    full_compiler_check_no_progress_over_five_minutes_2026-08-21, 0, "2026-11-28 p3sweep6: reproduced (scoped check --progress count: 340s wall, 0 check_phase events). Two root causes: (1) receipt emission gated only on --phase-profile - the --progress summary|count|dot option was validated (check_options.spl) and in --help but never consulted; (2) the composed entry sat silent across multi-minute chunk loads (worker output only printed on completion). Fix: wants_progress_receipts (main.spl) wires --progress to the designed per-file/per-phase receipts (none/no-progress/quiet default stay silent, --json still suppresses - pinned); check_entry.spl emits the check_phase receipt shape on stderr around every worker spawn (chunk_start/done + file_start/done, default-on summary). Verification: post-fix scoped matrix 6 invocations all pass; full-tree bare check ran 920s with 85 receipts, max inter-receipt gap 58s, done/total advancing; regression harness check_progress_receipts_test.shs PASS; check_phase_profile_test.shs PASS (contract preserved); entry specs 3/3 each. Residuals: per-file streaming inside a chunk needs process_run_timeout_live (Unix-only) - bounded by one worker invocation; the full-tree VERDICT still exceeds 15 min (separate deferred perf project); the new .shs shares the unwired-tests ledger entry. close_evidence reproducer=test/02_integration/app/check_progress_receipts_test.shs prevention=src/app/check/main.spl"

